# Settings for Phygital Engram. Copy this file to .env next to the program, or set these in your terminal.
# Everything here is optional. Every setting is explained in docs/settings.md.
# The names come from the working version and may change in later versions.
# Never put real values in this example file.

# ---- your notes ----
# The folder of Markdown notes to search. Phygital Engram only reads it.
# ENGRAM_VAULT=~/Notes

# ---- where its own files go ----
# The folder for the index. It must be OUTSIDE your notes folder, or it refuses to run.
# ENGRAM_DATA=~/.local/share/phygital-engram

# ---- note cards (optional) ----
# Your own AI key. Only used if you turn on note cards. Never share it, never commit it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- the connector for AI apps (optional) ----
# The path to engram.py, if it is not next to the mcp folder.
# PHYGITAL_ENGRAM_CLI=/path/to/phygital-engram/engram.py

# ---- the server version (mcp/serve.py), for your phone and the web ----
# Your domain, pointed at your server. The free HTTPS certificate is made for it.
# PHYGITAL_ENGRAM_DOMAIN=notes.example.com
# The folder on the server that holds your notes. It is mounted read-only.
# NOTES_DIR=/srv/notes
# Your passphrase, typed once on the login page. 8+ characters. Prefer LOGIN_HASH: run `python3 mcp/serve.py hash`.
# LOGIN_HASH=
# LOGIN_PASSPHRASE=
# How often to update the index, in minutes. 0 means never. Default 10.
# PHYGITAL_ENGRAM_REFRESH_MINUTES=10
# AI apps allowed to log in, as a comma list of hosts. Default: claude.ai, claude.com, chatgpt.com, openai.com, vscode.dev
# ALLOWED_REDIRECT_HOSTS=claude.ai,claude.com
# Set to 1 when a proxy such as Caddy sits in front (the Compose setup does this).
# PHYGITAL_ENGRAM_TRUST_PROXY=1

